"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[4320],{34320:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"inflyaciya-oktyabr-2026-tarify-zhkh","locale":"en","title":"Annual inflation jumps from 6.26% to 7.17% in a week after utility tariff indexation","description":"Prices rose by 0.96% from September 29 to October 5, 2026, with annual inflation at 7.17%. How much utility tariffs contributed and why the annual measure jumped in a week.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Russian consumer prices rose by 0.96% from September 29 to October 5, 2026, compared with 0.12% a week earlier. Utility tariff indexation from October 1 contributed 0.75 percentage points of that increase. Sewerage rose by 17.1%, cold water by 15.3%, hot water by 14.2%, heating by 12.7% and electricity by 12%. Overall utility bills were indexed by less, a nationwide average of 9.9%: the government sets that index for the total payment rather than each service. Moscow\'s limit is up to 15%, St Petersburg\'s up to 14.6%, and Stavropol Territory\'s is the highest at up to 22%."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Excluding utilities, prices rose by 0.21% over the week, faster than the entire basket had risen the week before. Food prices increased by 0.17%: fruit and vegetables fell by 0.57%, while other foods rose by 0.24%. Eggs increased by 2.2%, canned meat by 1.6% and buckwheat by 1%. Nonfood goods rose by 0.13%, smartphones by 1.1% and televisions by 1%."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Annual inflation rose from 6.26% to 7.17% in a week. Imagine a family paying car insurance once a year, in July last year but October this year. October spending looks higher against the previous year even though the annual total is unchanged. Utility tariffs work similarly: they rose by 11.9% on July 1, 2025, and in 2026 by 1.7% in January and 9.9% in October, about 11.8% combined. There was no tariff change in October 2025, so the entire current jump entered the annual comparison. This is the base effect. From 2027, tariff increases will return to July."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"If the utility portion of a monthly bill was 6 thousand rubles, it rose by about 600 rubles on average, or up to 900 in Moscow. Building maintenance and major repairs are outside this indexation. This spending cannot be postponed. Deposit rates still exceed price growth: the average maximum rate at the 10 largest banks was 13.05% in late September, versus annual inflation of 7.17%."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Bank of Russia expects 2026 inflation of 6–7%. Prices have risen by 5.94% since the start of the year, while annual inflation under the regulator\'s methodology is 7.08%, already above the upper end of its year-end forecast. Central bank adviser Kirill Tremasov had estimated the tariff contribution at about 0.7 points in September, so other prices matter more for the October 23 rate decision. A weekly pace of 0.21%, if sustained for a full year, would exceed 11%. On September 11, the Bank of Russia kept its rate at 14% and warned that inflation-acceleration risks predominated."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"One week proves little. Rosstat will publish September monthly data on October 9 and the next weekly data on October 14. If growth excluding tariffs returns to 0.1% a week, the jump will prove temporary. If it stays around 0.2%, the Bank of Russia will have fewer reasons to cut rates, leaving loans expensive and deposits attractive for longer."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did weekly inflation rise to 0.96% in early October 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Utility tariffs were indexed from October 1 by an average of 9.9%. This contributed 0.75 percentage points of the 0.96% rise. Excluding utilities, weekly prices increased by 0.21%."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Why did annual inflation jump from 6.26% to 7.17% in a week?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Because of the base effect. Utility tariffs rose by 11.9% on July 1, 2025, whereas in 2026 they rose by 1.7% in January and 9.9% from October 1. There was no tariff change in October 2025, so the year-on-year comparison sharply increased the annual reading even though total tariff growth will be almost the same, about 11.8%."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"How much did utility bills rise from October 1, 2026?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Overall utility payments rose by a nationwide average of 9.9%, up to 15% in Moscow, 14.6% in St Petersburg and 22% in Stavropol Territory. Building maintenance and major repairs are excluded. Among individual services, weekly sewerage prices rose by 17.1%, cold water by 15.3%, heating by 12.7% and electricity by 12%."}],"sources":[{"label":"Russian inflation from September 29 to October 5","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/10/07/1235202-inflyatsiya-v-rossii"},{"label":"Economy Ministry estimates utility indexation\'s weekly inflation contribution at 0.75 percentage points","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/10/07/1235205-minek-otsenil-vklad-indeksatsii"},{"label":"Utility indexation contributes an estimated 0.75 percentage points to weekly inflation","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1120937"},{"label":"Economy Ministry: annual Russian inflation reaches 7.17% from September 29 to October 5","url":"https://www.bfm.ru/news/620178"},{"label":"Utility tariffs from October 1, 2026: how bills change","url":"https://finuslugi.ru/navigator/kak-ehto-rabotaet/stat_tarify-zhkkh-s-1-oktyabrya-2026-goda-kak-izmenyatsya-platezhi"},{"label":"Weekly Russian inflation jumps 0.96% following tariff indexation","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/07/nedelnaya-inflyatsiya-v-rf-podskochila-na-096-iz-za-indeksatsii-tarifov-a208051"},{"label":"Bank of Russia raises its 2026 inflation forecast","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/8843971"},{"label":"Central bank holds its key rate at 14% on September 11, 2026","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/stavka-centrobanka-neizmenna-14-kak-reshenie-soveta-direktorov-cb-povliyaet-na-ekonomiku-69227357/"},{"label":"Average maximum deposit rate at ten banks rises to 13.05%","url":"https://ria.ru/20261001/bank-2121443529.html"}],"sourceBodySha256":"2123f3266d3346c5a40c0ca0051d02fcbfdc4a0c1b55fe5c397edea22f975b4d"}')}}]);